\ul{
\li{\strong{The geometric mean of the eight warm passes is 0.957 of the base's, and every corpus is faster}: Init 3.7 \%, Std 3.2 \%, cedar 1.2 \%, reachability 15.5 \%, con-leche 4.8 \%, navier-stokes-euler 2.1 \%, cslib 1.9 \%, Mathlib 1.3 \% (14.81 to 14.62 s). The CPU ratios of the 24 rounds are all below 1, between 0.825 and 0.992, and those of one corpus lie within 1.5 points of each other except cedar's (0.966 to 0.992).}
\li{\strong{reachability} is two units with sessions of hundreds of thousands of records: there the young tables answer most probes and the old ones are entered in batches (its tables were the case the young set was proposed for). Its pass is 0.54 s, so by the rule its figure is the mean of the warm passes.}
\li{\strong{Peak resident memory} is within 2 \% on every corpus (Mathlib 4,385 and 4,372 MiB).}
}
}

